  "stimuli": [
    {
      "stimulusId": "stim.a.reading.r1",
      "formId": "form-a",
      "domain": "reading",
      "kind": "PASSAGE",
      "title": "Borrowing tools from a library",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "paragraphId": "stim.a.reading.r1.p1",
          "text": "Northbridge Library has added a small tool-lending service to its book collection. Residents can borrow items such as hand saws and electric drills for occasional household jobs. The service is intended to reduce the need to buy equipment that might otherwise remain unused for months. It began as a ten-week trial, not as a promise to supply every tool a resident might need."
        },
        {
          "paragraphId": "stim.a.reading.r1.p2",
          "text": "Borrowers reserve tools through the library catalogue and return them to a staffed desk. Before borrowing an electric drill, a resident must attend a short safety demonstration, even if that person has used a drill before. Hand tools do not require this demonstration. The library chose a modest initial collection so that staff could inspect each returned item before lending it again."
        },
        {
          "paragraphId": "stim.a.reading.r1.p3",
          "text": "During the first month, the tools were borrowed sixty times. Organisers considered this encouraging, but they did not count sixty avoided purchases. Some borrowers might have hired a tool, borrowed one from a friend or postponed the job if the service had not existed. Loan records alone therefore could not show how many new purchases the service had prevented."
        },
        {
          "paragraphId": "stim.a.reading.r1.p4",
          "text": "At the end of the trial, staff will compare loan records with borrowers' comments. Frequently requested tools may be added, while little-used items may be removed. Volunteers can help describe tools in the catalogue, but trained staff will remain responsible for safety checks. The organisers want the collection to respond to actual use while keeping responsibility for its condition clear."
        }
      ],
      "provenanceId": "source-authoring",
      "fictionalContext": true
    },
